# the docs module's law fragment: the docs discipline, composed into the generated layer
@append @laws
  docs-first: prompt -> map -> doc -> code behavioral first move: every task begins with the whole picture, the index (ctx docs query --index: the repos and units that exist; read whole, never capped; the boot clause names the exact complete marker) and the general-level docs (workspace conventions, the repo's overview and operational docs), before any specific lookup; then the owning doc: the query line -> doc -> section; read code only for what the doc lacked; the doc is ground truth, trust or fix, never work around; a read the docs do not serve is correct (census, existence, enumeration, absence); docs rank, cap and explain, they never count; doc vs code: code wins on what IS, the doc on why and intent; no question to the human the docs answer; TEST: would the doc have answered this? yes -> stop reading code
  docs-are-code: a doc'd change lands with its doc update, same change, on the spot, never deferred; git versions the code and the guides; the corpus lives in the configured store and every corpus write goes through the ctx docs write verbs (a write any other way skips the grammar check, so it is drift; under a store driver the change log stamps each write with the workspace git HEAD); nothing waits; close-time verifies, it never updates; a doc-vs-code conflict you notice is real, the doc fix rides the same change
  git-dependency: the docs module requires git: the change-aware verbs, the check, the gate, and the drift read git's delta; the change log stamps each write with the workspace git HEAD; a workspace without git loses the change-aware checks while the audit, the query, and the writes stand
  corpus-untracked: the agent-facing corpus is never committed: under the files driver it is gitignored working state, under a store driver it lives in the store alone; the guides (docs/*.md plus README.md) stay tracked files, synced by the workspace's own rule
  corpus-reconcile: code moves reconcile the corpus via the docs-drift flow, never from memory; the audit stays live over the corpus; under the files driver the check's untracked-claimant verdict (CLEAN (PROCESS-OWNED)) hands the reconciliation to the process; under a store driver the change log feeds the gate's corpus half and the check enforces freshness from each doc's own sources
  gap: a path no doc owns, or a doc that lags code, is a finding; stub it or record the gap in the same unit of work, silence is the only failure; what the doc lacked is the finding, name and capture it; promote it into the owning doc, the update is the promotion; the contract vocab lives in the docs module's grammar, one home
  harness-free: the agent's docs duties never assume the harness; the contract runs on plain POSIX tools and the ctx verbs, over plain files under the files driver
  docs-audience-separation: documentation surfaces split by audience: user-facing guides (docs/*.md, README.md) own the product depth and low-level physical implementation details (disk layout, file formats, runtime internals) for human maintainers; the agent-facing corpus (what ctx docs serves, held by the configured storage driver) owns the operational contracts, abstract surfaces, and CLI interfaces for agent execution; the agent-facing corpus must remain strictly conceptual and tooling-first, describing surfaces and commands without exposing physical disk paths, filenames, or storage layouts.

@append @layout
  the corpus conventions (repo workspace, slug conventions): the universal rules for the corpus, read through ctx docs query workspace conventions under any driver

@append @boot
  before the first specific lookup: the cross-repo overview map via ctx docs query --index, the index read whole (it ends with "index complete: N entries"; a missing marker means it was truncated, re-read it whole), then the general-level docs: the workspace conventions and the entering repo's overview and operational docs

@append @close
  docs gate (unit close): at the unit close's gate step, ctx docs gate must pass cleanly, chaining the audit (the corpus grammar and integrity) and the check (coverage completeness and doc freshness); a unit does not close red; the gate verifies change, never truth
